@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] trace-spool-accepted-custody
A successful admission MUST follow exclusive private custody, initial directory fsync,
and SQLite WAL transactions with synchronous=FULL fsync. Accepted batches MUST remain immutable
and retained until configured expiry even after Collector or Tempo acknowledgment.
ACK loss MUST preserve the same batch; uncertain storage MUST poison admission.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] trace-spool-provenance
Admission MUST validate kernel UID, exact systemd service cgroup and stable
process incarnation. The spool MUST replace resource provenance and accept only
the reviewed name/attribute schema. Raw payloads, exception text, status messages,
events, baggage and arbitrary resource identity MUST NOT reach upstream.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] trace-spool-refuses-new-data
Archive quota exhaustion MUST refuse new data without evicting accepted batches.
Telemetry failure MUST NOT signal or restart the producer, mutate application
authority or inspect its command arguments, terminal or disk streams.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] trace-spool-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover: sanitize refusal of unreviewed attribute keys for
arbitrary string values; the schema attribute closure over arbitrary keys (uuid
keys accepted iff an independent UUID oracle agrees, enum keys only with reviewed
values, numeric keys only with non-negative integers, all else refused); body-limit
and empty-body refusal in sanitize and accept, plus accept's zero-clock and
retention-overflow refusal with unchanged custody; `sql` accepting exactly the
signed SQLite range and round-tripping through SQLite via `number`; `digest` and
the accept identity against an independent SHA-256; and archive survival across
ACK loss, delivery, reopen with a shorter retention, replay and expiry.
